# The XPI is a zip of the working-tree files, so the published SHA-256 depends
# on their exact bytes. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which
# would hand a Windows clone CRLF line endings and change every text file —
# verified: a CRLF checkout builds a different hash and a different size.
# Pinning the working tree to LF everywhere is what makes "byte-reproducible on
# any machine" true rather than "on any Unix machine".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending-convert binaries.
*.png binary
*.xpi binary
*.zip binary
